\section{What this gives us, and what it does not}

\subsection{What we have}
\begin{itemize}
  \item \textbf{A model with traceable verification checks.} Every capability of the
    solver has a rung that isolates it and a number that checks it. When
    something breaks later, \texttt{./Allrun-ladder 012-024} reruns all
    checks and points at the first rung that fails.
  \item \textbf{Nothing goes missing.} The recorded pair and element ledgers close near
    round-off in the cited cases. These checks address conservation, not
    the adequacy of the physical model.
  \item \textbf{A useful prediction.} Against five experiments the
    untuned model halves the error in \Tdep{} of the published models
    (18\,K vs 35\,K RMS), and it reproduces the multi-band deposits of the
    LBE experiments.
  \item \textbf{A paper trail.} Cases 023 and 024 feed directly into the
    methods manuscript (Sec.~6.3, Table~V, Fig.~5) and the ladder is the
    availability section of LESTO deliverable D38.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{What we do not have yet}
\begin{itemize}
  \item Some inputs of the experiments are not published and are
    \emph{assumed}: how fast the boat released its material, the reference
    conditions of the flow, and several positions. The 024 results are
    therefore labelled provisional.
  \item The model's deposit peaks sit 1 to 4\,cm upstream of the measured
    ones in 023; the boat's obstruction of the flow and the dense vapour
    right next to it are not represented.
  \item The \BiI{} cases (018, 019, 021) need restricted thermodynamic
    tables that cannot be redistributed, and 015 and 020 need an optional
    GEMS3K build; without them those cases print \texttt{NOTRUN}.
  \item The mesh study of 024 shows small changes (1.98\,\%) but no formal
    grid-convergence index: the apparent orders of convergence are not
    consistent.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Points to discuss with Bojan}
\begin{enumerate}
 \item Confirm the original T-Flows inputs for Figs.~8--10: the imposed
 onset temperature, wall-layer thickness and rate parameters. This would
 resolve the case-022 onset discrepancy at its source.
 \item Review the HKS units and pressure convention in both implementations,
 and compare the same interface law before attributing differences to
 the flow solver. The physical runs here use SI units and Eq.~\eqref{eq:resistance}.
 \item Prioritise the remaining input uncertainties: boat release history,
 flow reference conditions and boat position. Compare complete deposit
 profiles as well as the 1\,\% onset when assessing improvements.
\end{enumerate}

\begin{inshort}[How to try it]
Every case lives in \texttt{run/<NNN-name>/}. Read its \texttt{readme.md},
then run \texttt{./Allrun} (cases 012--024; outputs go into a
git-ignored \texttt{work/} folder) and look for \texttt{PASS}. The cheap
cases take seconds to minutes; 017 about 8 minutes; the full 023 and 024
studies take hours per experiment. The slide-by-slide version of this
report is \texttt{presentations/case-ladder/lesto-case-ladder.pdf}.
\end{inshort}

